{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"simious-comic-marmot","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nDuring the comment-remediation Group17 full `make verify` run on macOS/Git 2.56, `tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py::test_write_survives_foreground_maintenance_repack` failed because the ticket-create `git commit` exceeded its monkeypatched `_GIT_TIMEOUT=1.0`. The same unchanged test passed in 163.96 seconds isolated and again in 44.00 seconds with Git Trace2 under concurrent suites; the latter measured both ticket-create commits at 0.015 seconds each. The Group17 patch changes only comments in other files and preserves normalized AST. At the check, host load averages were 18.13/21.83/22.56, but the failed run has no Git trace, so the cause is unproven.\n\n## Hypotheses and distinguishing check\nCompeting explanations: host scheduling or disk contention delayed a normally short commit; Git or test state occasionally triggers extra work; another changing condition. Run the targeted test with Git Trace2 during controlled low- and high-activity periods, record commit wall time and Git child processes, then determine whether 1 second is a valid stable bound for this invariant. Do not classify a passing retry as a diagnosis.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\nRecord a reproducible cause or a bounded measurement series that distinguishes the explanations; fix the underlying code or the test's timing design without weakening the assertion that commit auto-maintenance is suppressed; run the targeted test under relevant load and the full `make verify` gate. Keep this bug separate from the comment-only Gerrit change.","id":"99fb-a2f3-3e9d-4116","parent_id":"","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["bug","flaky-test","testing"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fixed 1-second Git commit bound fails under concurrent full-suite load"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792778374460996380,"uuid":"b64cede5-48b3-48eb-9989-18d1f96ed448"}